Right --- it would be possible to parallelize likelihood computations
by dividing the data.  We'd need to build up a TensorFlow-like interface
that allows us to specify comptuation units in terms of input arguments
that returns a value with partials that can be slotted back into the global
autodiff graph.  The trick will be figuring out how to deal with memory
efficiently for subcomputations.

I'm going to the autodiff workshop in September---maybe they'll have
some good ideas about parallelization techniques.

- Bob

