For example, I wanted to open a question about the currently implementation of one/two compartment models is very clearly coded around oral dosing, with CL/V/K. For example, https://github.com/charlesm93/math/blob/feature/issue-314-torsten-pharmacometrics/stan/math/torsten/PKModel/PKModel_class.hpp#L54 shows onecmpt having two compartments, which for oral given the depot compartment makes complete sense, however when managing IV you don't need that depot. This goes in the other direction, like if you have multiple depot compartments for complex absorption models

Do you have any spec docs or otherwise to expand on the thought process behind some of these implementation details, as well as get a better understanding of the overall implementation without tracing through the code itself. For example, I was trying to find some more detail about things like handling parameterizations (physiological CL/Ka/V vs rate constants).

Really excited about this implementation - great work so far!

