Hi Sebastian,

> I am wondering if we should make the wiki around "complex ODE" models instead of being domain specific on Pharmacometrics.

I think we could have two wikis and make the distinction between generalizable features and pharmacometrics specific ones. I'm with you on keeping in mind applications to other fields. Are there particular cases in System Biology you are thinking about? I think an example would give me a better sense of what is generalizable vs what is PKPD specific.

> Is there an example program I can try with Torsten?

I forked example-models (here <https://github.com/charlesm93/example-models/tree/feature/issue-70-PKPDexamples-torsten/PKPD/torsten>). I need to add a summary of outcome and some documentation before submitting a pull request. I will probably share one or two more examples to illustrate more features. I also work with a nice R setup to simulate data, run Stan, and then do posterior predictive checks -- this might be worth sharing.

> I would advise you to think at the moment about tests, but hold off for the moment to implement all of them.

I will follow your advice. As I see it, the next step is to discuss design during a Stan meeting. Any idea which week this could happen on? I should be flexible, and I would feel best in both Bill and Sebastian were present (in person or electronically).

best,
charles

